{
  "tanrei": {
    "sys": {
      "motion": {
        "$extensions": {
          "dev.tanrei.llm": {
            "usage": "Durations by role (role.*, multiples of dial.motion.unit), curves by role (easing.enter, exit, state, spatial) over a scale of curves and springs, and where a surface that appears starts from (appear.*, set by sys.behavior.appearance). A component times and eases a change by its role; a product re-times or re-eases a role in one line.",
            "rules": [
              "Respect reduced motion: platforms skip or shorten transitions; never rely on motion to convey state.",
              "A component token for a duration or a curve aliases a role (role.*, easing.enter, easing.exit, easing.state, easing.spatial), not a step of the duration scale or a curve of the scale: the scale and the springs are what the roles are made of.",
              "A surface that leaves eases by easing.exit and takes its role's exit duration, which is shorter than its enter duration.",
              "appear.* holds where a surface that appears starts from; set sys.behavior.appearance to change them together, or pin one of them."
            ]
          }
        },
        "duration": {
          "$type": "duration",
          "short1": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 50,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 1
              }
            }
          },
          "short2": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 100,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 2
              }
            }
          },
          "short3": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 150,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 3
              }
            }
          },
          "short4": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 200,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 4
              }
            }
          },
          "medium1": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 250,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 5
              }
            }
          },
          "medium2": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 300,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 6
              }
            }
          },
          "medium3": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 350,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 7
              }
            }
          },
          "medium4": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 400,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 8
              }
            }
          },
          "long1": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 450,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 9
              }
            }
          },
          "long2": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 500,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 10
              }
            }
          },
          "long3": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 550,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 11
              }
            }
          },
          "long4": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 600,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 12
              }
            }
          },
          "extra-long1": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 700,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 14
              }
            }
          },
          "extra-long2": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 800,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 16
              }
            }
          },
          "extra-long3": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 900,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 18
              }
            }
          },
          "extra-long4": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 1000,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 20
              }
            }
          },
          "stagger": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 100,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$description": "Delay between items in a sequential reveal.",
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 2
              }
            }
          },
          "press-hold": {
            "$value": {
              "value": 100,
              "unit": "ms"
            },
            "$description": "The shortest time a pressed state stays visible. A tap or a keyboard activation is over in a frame; without a floor the feedback cannot be seen.",
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "mul",
                "of": "{tanrei.dial.motion.unit}",
                "by": 2
              }
            }
          },
          "$extensions": {
            "dev.tanrei.vocabulary": {
              "rationale": "One product uses short durations for small state changes and longer ones for large surfaces entering or leaving.",
              "since": "0.1.0"
            }
          }
        },
        "role": {
          "$type": "duration",
          "$description": "How long a motion takes, by what moves — its role — rather than by a step of the duration scale. A component's duration token aliases the role of the change it animates, so every component of a role keeps one pace and a product re-times the role in one line. The values follow dial.motion.unit.",
          "state": {
            "compact": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short3}",
              "$description": "A change of state — hover, focus, press — of a small control: a checkbox's box, an icon button, a small button, a chip.",
              "$extensions": {}
            },
            "default": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short3}",
              "$description": "A change of state of a control of medium size: a button, a text field.",
              "$extensions": {}
            },
            "large": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short3}",
              "$description": "A change of state of a large surface: a list row, a card, a table's row, a navigation item.",
              "$extensions": {}
            }
          },
          "selection": {
            "mark": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.spring.standard.fast-effects.duration}",
              "$description": "A selection mark that appears in place: a check mark, a radio button's dot.",
              "$extensions": {}
            },
            "travel": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.spring.standard.fast-spatial.duration}",
              "$description": "A selection that travels: a switch's handle, the indicator of tabs or of a navigation bar.",
              "$extensions": {}
            }
          },
          "resize": {
            "default": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short4}",
              "$description": "A box that changes its size in place: a text field that grows by a line, an error line that opens below a field.",
              "$extensions": {}
            },
            "large": {
              "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.spring.standard.default-spatial.duration}",
              "$description": "A large change of size: an attachment strip that opens, a row added to or taken out of a list.",
              "$extensions": {}
            }
          },
          "disclosure": {
            "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.spring.standard.fast-spatial.duration}",
            "$description": "Content that opens and closes in place: an accordion's panel, a tree's group, a section of a drawer.",
            "$extensions": {}
          },
          "appear": {
            "hint": {
              "enter": {
                "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short4}",
                "$description": "A hint beside what it describes (a tooltip) appears.",
                "$extensions": {}
              },
              "exit": {
                "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short3}",
                "$description": "A hint beside what it describes (a tooltip) leaves. Leaving is shorter than appearing.",
                "$extensions": {}
              }
            },
            "anchored": {
              "enter": {
                "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short4}",
                "$description": "A surface anchored to what opened it (a menu, a select's or a combobox's list, a popover, a docked picker) appears.",
                "$extensions": {}
              },
              "exit": {
                "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short2}",
                "$description": "A surface anchored to what opened it (a menu, a select's or a combobox's list, a popover, a docked picker) leaves. Leaving is shorter than appearing.",
                "$extensions": {}
              }
            },
            "modal": {
              "enter": {
                "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.medium2}",
                "$description": "A modal surface over the page, and the scrim behind it (a dialog, a modal picker, an image preview) appears.",
                "$extensions": {}
              },
              "exit": {
                "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short4}",
                "$description": "A modal surface over the page, and the scrim behind it (a dialog, a modal picker, an image preview) leaves. Leaving is shorter than appearing.",
                "$extensions": {}
              }
            },
            "sheet": {
              "enter": {
                "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.medium2}",
                "$description": "A sheet that slides in from an edge (a bottom sheet, a side sheet, a modal drawer) appears.",
                "$extensions": {}
              },
              "exit": {
                "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short4}",
                "$description": "A sheet that slides in from an edge (a bottom sheet, a side sheet, a modal drawer) leaves. Leaving is shorter than appearing.",
                "$extensions": {}
              }
            },
            "toast": {
              "enter": {
                "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.medium1}",
                "$description": "A message at an edge of the window that leaves on its own (a snackbar) appears.",
                "$extensions": {}
              },
              "exit": {
                "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short3}",
                "$description": "A message at an edge of the window that leaves on its own (a snackbar) leaves. Leaving is shorter than appearing.",
                "$extensions": {}
              }
            }
          },
          "feedback": {
            "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.long1}",
            "$description": "The answer to a press that spreads from the point of contact (a ripple).",
            "$extensions": {}
          },
          "show-delay": {
            "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.medium2}",
            "$description": "How long a loading indicator or a skeleton waits before it appears, so that a short wait shows nothing at all.",
            "$extensions": {}
          },
          "reduced": {
            "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.duration.short2}",
            "$description": "The cross-fade that takes the place of a movement, a scaling or a blur while motion is reduced.",
            "$extensions": {}
          },
          "$extensions": {
            "dev.tanrei.vocabulary": {
              "rationale": "One product times its motions by what moves: a tooltip appears faster than a dialog, a check mark settles faster than a sheet slides in, and every component that does the same kind of thing keeps the same pace. Without roles a product re-times one kind of motion component by component, and components of one kind drift apart.",
              "since": "0.1.0"
            }
          }
        },
        "easing": {
          "$type": "cubicBezier",
          "standard": {
            "$value": [
              0.2,
              0,
              0,
              1
            ],
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fixed": "A curve is a shape, not a quantity a dial can scale."
              }
            }
          },
          "standard-decelerate": {
            "$value": [
              0,
              0,
              0,
              1
            ],
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fixed": "A curve is a shape, not a quantity a dial can scale."
              }
            }
          },
          "standard-accelerate": {
            "$value": [
              0.3,
              0,
              1,
              1
            ],
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fixed": "A curve is a shape, not a quantity a dial can scale."
              }
            }
          },
          "emphasized-decelerate": {
            "$value": [
              0.05,
              0.7,
              0.1,
              1
            ],
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fixed": "A curve is a shape, not a quantity a dial can scale."
              }
            }
          },
          "emphasized-accelerate": {
            "$value": [
              0.3,
              0,
              0.8,
              0.15
            ],
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fixed": "A curve is a shape, not a quantity a dial can scale."
              }
            }
          },
          "linear": {
            "$value": [
              0,
              0,
              1,
              1
            ],
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fixed": "A curve is a shape, not a quantity a dial can scale."
              }
            }
          },
          "enter": {
            "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.easing.emphasized-decelerate}",
            "$description": "The curve of a surface that appears: quick at first, settling into place.",
            "$extensions": {}
          },
          "exit": {
            "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.easing.emphasized-accelerate}",
            "$description": "The curve of a surface that leaves: it gathers speed as it goes, so little of the surface is left on its last frame (about 7–9 % of its opacity at 250–350 ms).",
            "$extensions": {}
          },
          "state": {
            "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.easing.standard}",
            "$description": "The curve of a change of state in place: a color, an opacity, a mark.",
            "$extensions": {}
          },
          "spatial": {
            "$value": "{tanrei.sys.motion.spring.standard.fast-spatial.easing}",
            "$description": "The curve of something that moves or changes its size in place: a switch's handle, the indicator of tabs, a box that grows.",
            "$extensions": {}
          },
          "$extensions": {
            "dev.tanrei.vocabulary": {
              "rationale": "One product eases entrances, exits and on-screen moves differently.",
              "since": "0.1.0"
            }
          }
        },
        "appear": {
          "$description": "Where a surface that appears starts from, and where one that leaves ends: its opacity, its scale, how far it travels and how blurred it is — one appearance for every surface that appears (a menu, a select's list, a popover, a tooltip, a dialog, a snackbar). The values follow sys.behavior.appearance: a layer chooses the appearance, or pins one value. A sheet slides in from its edge whatever the appearance.",
          "opacity": {
            "$type": "number",
            "$value": 0,
            "$description": "The opacity a surface starts from as it appears and ends at as it leaves: 0 fades it; 1 does not.",
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "pick",
                "by": "{tanrei.sys.behavior.appearance}",
                "values": {
                  "fade-scale": 0,
                  "fade": 0,
                  "fade-slide": 0,
                  "blur-slide": 0,
                  "unfold": 0
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "scale": {
            "$type": "number",
            "$value": 0,
            "$description": "The scale a surface starts from as it appears, toward its origin: 0.96 grows it a little into place; 1 does not scale it. Under unfold the scale applies only along the axis that leaves the anchor, so the surface unfolds from its anchored edge.",
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "pick",
                "by": "{tanrei.sys.behavior.appearance}",
                "values": {
                  "fade-scale": 0.96,
                  "fade": 1,
                  "fade-slide": 1,
                  "blur-slide": 1,
                  "unfold": 0
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "distance": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "$value": {
              "value": 0,
              "unit": "px"
            },
            "$description": "How far a surface travels into place as it appears. The component gives the direction: away from its anchor for an anchored surface.",
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "pick",
                "by": "{tanrei.sys.behavior.appearance}",
                "values": {
                  "fade-scale": {
                    "value": 0,
                    "unit": "px"
                  },
                  "fade": {
                    "value": 0,
                    "unit": "px"
                  },
                  "fade-slide": "{tanrei.sys.space.space100}",
                  "blur-slide": "{tanrei.sys.space.space100}",
                  "unfold": {
                    "value": 0,
                    "unit": "px"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "blur": {
            "$type": "dimension",
            "$value": {
              "value": 0,
              "unit": "px"
            },
            "$description": "How blurred a surface starts as it appears; it comes into focus as it arrives.",
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fn": "pick",
                "by": "{tanrei.sys.behavior.appearance}",
                "values": {
                  "fade-scale": {
                    "value": 0,
                    "unit": "px"
                  },
                  "fade": {
                    "value": 0,
                    "unit": "px"
                  },
                  "fade-slide": {
                    "value": 0,
                    "unit": "px"
                  },
                  "blur-slide": {
                    "value": 4,
                    "unit": "px"
                  },
                  "unfold": {
                    "value": 0,
                    "unit": "px"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "origin": {
            "$type": "number",
            "$value": 0,
            "$description": "Where an anchored surface grows from. anchor: the middle of its edge that faces what opened it. center: its own centre. A modal surface grows from its centre whatever the choice.",
            "$extensions": {
              "dev.tanrei.enum": {
                "values": [
                  "anchor",
                  "center"
                ]
              },
              "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                "fixed": "A choice of kind; no dial scales it."
              },
              "dev.tanrei.vocabulary": {
                "rationale": "One product grows its menus and popovers out of what opened them — a menu unfolds from its button — where another grows each of them from its own centre, as a card that hovers into place does. It is one decision for every anchored surface of the product.",
                "since": "0.1.0"
              }
            }
          },
          "$extensions": {
            "dev.tanrei.vocabulary": {
              "rationale": "One product makes everything that appears appear the same way: its menu, its tooltip and its dialog fade and grow alike, and a product whose surfaces travel or come into focus wants that everywhere. Where a surface starts from is decided once and read by every surface; without it each surface restates it and they drift apart.",
              "since": "0.1.0"
            }
          }
        },
        "spring": {
          "$description": "Motion physics. \"spatial\" moves things (may overshoot); \"effects\" changes color/opacity (never overshoots). `standard` is the default scheme; `expressive` is the additive layer.",
          "standard": {
            "fast-spatial": {
              "damping": {
                "$type": "number",
                "$value": 0.9,
                "$extensions": {
                  "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                    "fixed": "Spring physics do not scale linearly with the speed dial."
                  }
                }
              },
              "stiffness": {
                "$type": "number",
                "$value": 1400,
                "$extensions": {
                  "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                    "fixed": "Spring physics do not scale linearly with the speed dial."
                  }
                }
              },
              "easing": {
                "$type": "cubicBezier",
                "$value": [
                  0.27,
                  1.06,
                  0.18,
                  1
                ],
                "$description": "Approximation for platforms without spring animations (CSS).",
                "$extensions": {
                  "dev.tanrei.derive": {
                    "fixed": "A curve is a shape, not a quantity a dial can scale."
                  }
                }
              },
              "duration": {
                "$type": "duration",
                "$value": {
                  "value": 350,
                  "unit": "ms"
                },
                "$extensions": {
                  "dev.tanrei.derive": {
